From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] OWE: Fix ECDH copy in association request parsing

PeerAssocReqCmmSanity() copies the received ECDH element through the
single-byte ext_id_ecdh member, spanning the group and public key.
The existing length check bounds this copy to ecdh_ie, but kernel
FORTIFY reports a field-spanning write when an OWE station associates.

Copying the complete element, including its header, into ecdh_ie avoids
the field-spanning write. The existing capacity check covers this copy
and the stored bytes remain unchanged.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt_wifi/common/fsm/ap_mgmt_assoc.c
+++ b/mt_wifi/common/fsm/ap_mgmt_assoc.c
@@ -1585,9 +1585,7 @@ BOOLEAN PeerAssocReqCmmSanity
 					break;
 				}
 				os_zero_mem(&ie_lists->ecdh_ie, sizeof(ie_lists->ecdh_ie));
-				ie_lists->ecdh_ie.ext_ie_id = IE_WLAN_EXTENSION;
-				ie_lists->ecdh_ie.length = eid_ptr->Len;
-				NdisMoveMemory(&ie_lists->ecdh_ie.ext_id_ecdh, eid_ptr->Octet, eid_ptr->Len);
+				NdisMoveMemory(&ie_lists->ecdh_ie, eid_ptr, eid_ptr->Len + 2);
 			}
 #endif /*CONFIG_OWE_SUPPORT*/
 				break;
